at he can actually move on  from it  without a doubt my favorite scene in the  entire episode is the closing shot  we had this long shot of molly sitting  on the little wall  gordo walks up and asked to bum a  cigarette without saying anything she  just pulls one out  lights it for him hands it off he sits  down and it's just perfect and this is  really the moment i realized that all  that character work that they did in  season one is finally paying off  i like these guys flaws and all they're  all right with me  so we don't get a lot of karen in this  episode or really much ed on his own  either but we do get some scenes with  their daughter their adopted daughter  who we know nothing about  she's just sort of there right now at  this point this is probably what i was  least interested in in this episode  this and the stephen's kids as well i  imagine that this is also setting up  something in the future  similar to what i was talking about with  the elita stuff in season one  it just feels a little out of place at  this point  and we do get a little bit of tracy we  see that she's doing a modeling gig  she's wearing her suit she's probably  getting paid pretty good money for this  padding out that government paycheck she  seems happy  we know she got married we see the ring  again  things seem to be going pretty good in  that part of her life she seems to be  ducking her  responsibilities a little bit in her  astronaut training  that may come up later but there is  tension between her and  ed in relation to her not telling gordo  about getting married  before she announced it on tv so it's a  little hard to see  where they're going with tracy at this  point she does have a cell phone that  was kind of fun to see  maybe those are more accessible more  common in the 1983 alternate timeline  and that's really all there is i can say  about what happened given that it is a  setup episode  they needed to get gordo and danny back  in training  and get ready to send them back to the  moon it's interesting that gordo  is clearly not happy doing what he's  doing we see him talking to some  shriners here  he looks like he's put on about 40  pounds he's drinking heavily  but what's interesting is he prefers  that over the idea of going back to the  moon he's terrified of that  from what we can gather danny seems a  lot more gung-ho  as far as the events in her private life  it looks like this is something that  really means something to her  and we can't forget about the fact that  she made a real sacrifice for gordo the  last time they were there  so i like the setup some other things  that i wanted to mention  man there are so many people on  jamestown base this thing is fully  staffed at this point  it's something to see really and i liked  watching ellen say goodbye to it  she helped build it she's been there  she's put in time there  it's a part of who she is and i thought  you could feel that when she was getting  ready to leave  she's telling herself i have this other  stuff to do on earth i think i can be of  more use there but you can see that she  has real feelings about the base  about leaving the moon behind and we can  imagine that applies to everybody  i also like that she's the advocate for  the mars missions i think we're gonna  see movement there  i think it's inevitable that there will  be a mars program  maybe not this season but it is  something that will have to happen  and it's good to know that she'll be  involved with that we heard other  mentions of the pathfinder shuttle there  was talk of putting missiles on board  which is on hold for now according to  payne  but i feel like there's some big reveals  coming in that part of the story we're  gonna see them continue to progress  new technology new missions see how the  space program  develops under these different  circumstances  and i'm excited to see it i think that's  a good place to leave things  we could pick up the discussion in the  comments let me know 